language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Discrete tomography: reconstruct a 0/1 matrix from the number of ones in each row and in each column.
given row_sums_dim1 : int(1..)
given col_sums_dim1 : int(1..)
given row_sums : matrix indexed by [int(1..row_sums_dim1)] of int(0..)
given col_sums : matrix indexed by [int(1..col_sums_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ the 0/1 matrix to reconstruct (matrix_ is the output named matrix)
find matrix_ : matrix indexed by [int(1..row_sums_dim1), int(1..col_sums_dim1)] of int(0..1)

branching on [matrix_]
such that
$ each row contains as many ones as its row sum
forAll r : int(1..row_sums_dim1) . ((sum c : int(1..col_sums_dim1) . matrix_[r,c]) = row_sums[r]),
$ each column contains as many ones as its column sum
forAll c : int(1..col_sums_dim1) . ((sum r : int(1..row_sums_dim1) . matrix_[r,c]) = col_sums[c])
